 The tragedy at Douglas High School has ignited cries of anger and calls for stronger gun control measures across the nation, but I have for years been outraged and called for such measures in response to the gun violence that takes place across out nation almost every day, particularly in urban communities. I am tired of burying black boys and young men. I am tired of comforting parents, siblings and other family members after these heinous and inexplicable acts of violence, said Congresswoman Wilson.
